## Skills

Repo-wide skills are an [APM](https://microsoft.github.io/apm/) package (`apm.yml`): source `.apm/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, installed `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (what agents read). Always-on rules are `.apm/instructions/*.instructions.md`; after editing them, run `apm install`, then `apm compile --target cursor --local-only --no-links --no-constitution` to regenerate Cursor rules and `AGENTS.md`. Cursor hooks are native (`.cursor/hooks.json`, `.cursor/hooks/`); APM does not manage them. In a monorepo, also `<project>/.agents/skills/` when present. When a task matches a skill description, read and follow the installed `SKILL.md`. **Before any commit**, read `.agents/skills/git-commits/SKILL.md` even if the user did not mention commits. After editing a skill, run `apm install`. Other repos: `weakish/vibe` (skills and instructions).

| Skill | Path |
|-------|------|
| Git commits and trailers | `.agents/skills/git-commits/SKILL.md` |
| Review one commit; fix after selection | `.agents/skills/review/SKILL.md` |
| Herdr (only when the user asks) | `.agents/skills/herdr/SKILL.md` |
